// Vùng đất: the pet goes out into a region and fights on its map in real time (the design the user approved,
// side-session-notes .../DE-XUAT_vung-dat.md, 2026-10-26). A region on the "Ra ngoài" map opens its gate scene; from
// there its khu, painted top-down maps of 1536x1024 drawn 1:1 with the camera on the pet, one after the other along
// the dirt path. Tà khí nests (the purple crystals and smoke of the painting, cut out by scripts/vung_dat.py) send
// out spirits of the region's element gone wild; the khu is cleansed when its nests are broken, and the last khu's
// boss comes out of its gate once they are. The pet fights with its own Solo pictures, made small for the map:
//   ◀▶▲▼ move · A strike (3-hit combo) · B element shot (Linh lực) · X / R1 / L1 dash · Y ultimate (Nộ full)
//   START pause · SELECT leave
// Its stats are the pet's six attributes (gems included) and level; a khu costs Năng lượng and No; EXP goes through
// gainExp (the hourly pool), gold and finds are banked when the trip ends. Progress (nests broken, bosses) is S.vung.
// Pictures (scripts/vung_dat.py -> img/vg/): the khu maps and nests, the gate scenes, every Solo pet's map body and
// effects. Speed on the R36S: the map is one 1:1 copy of the screen's part a frame; sprites are drawn 1:1 (made at
// their size once: the foes' tà khí tint and size when the khu loads), nothing turned or scaled in a frame.
